From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: jz4780: fill a channel's descriptor pool when it is requested

A transfer's descriptors are allocated with GFP_NOWAIT when it is prepared;
for audio that's in the PCM trigger, in atomic context. A pool block is a
whole page, and the pool starts empty, so the first audio start after boot
needed a fresh page from the page allocator. With the H2's 24 MiB, free
memory in the first seconds after boot can be below the min watermark (616
KiB), and the start failed: "ASoC error (-12): at soc_component_trigger()",
and the player's first write with it. Two blocks are now put in the pool
when the channel is requested (sleeping allowed); freed blocks stay in the
pool until it is destroyed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
@@ -112,6 +112,8 @@
 
 /* Size of allocations for hardware descriptor blocks. */
 #define JZ_DMA_DESC_BLOCK_SIZE	PAGE_SIZE
+/* blocks put in a channel's pool when it is requested (one in use, one ending) */
+#define JZ_DMA_PREALLOC_DESC	2
 #define JZ_DMA_MAX_DESC		\
 	(JZ_DMA_DESC_BLOCK_SIZE / sizeof(struct jz4780_dma_hwdesc))
 
@@ -770,6 +772,29 @@
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Descriptors are allocated with GFP_NOWAIT when a transfer is
+	 * prepared (for audio, in the PCM trigger, in atomic context), and a
+	 * pool block is a whole page: the first prepare after boot needed a
+	 * fresh page from the page allocator, and below the min watermark it
+	 * failed (ASoC error -12 at the first audio start). Fill the pool now,
+	 * while sleeping is allowed: freed blocks stay in the pool.
+	 */
+	{
+		void *blk[JZ_DMA_PREALLOC_DESC];
+		dma_addr_t phys[JZ_DMA_PREALLOC_DESC];
+		int i, n;
+
+		for (n = 0; n < JZ_DMA_PREALLOC_DESC; n++) {
+			blk[n] = dma_pool_alloc(jzchan->desc_pool, GFP_KERNEL,
+						&phys[n]);
+			if (!blk[n])
+				break;
+		}
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+			dma_pool_free(jzchan->desc_pool, blk[i], phys[i]);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
